# ============================================================================
# .dvcignore TEMPLATE
#
# Copied to <project>/.dvcignore by init-dvc.sh.
#
# Same syntax as .gitignore, but a different audience: this tells DVC which
# paths to skip when it walks a tracked folder to hash its contents.
#
# Why bother? `dvc add` on a large data directory has to read and checksum
# every file underneath it. Excluding junk makes that faster and keeps the
# junk out of the DVC cache and off the remote.
# ============================================================================


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Operating system metadata that sync clients scatter through data folders.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
._*
Thumbs.db
Desktop.ini


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Editor and tooling scratch files.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.ipynb_checkpoints/


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Temporary and partial files.
# Half-written downloads and intermediate scratch should not be checksummed
# into a data version — they are not part of the dataset.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.tmp
*.temp
*.partial
*.crdownload
*.part


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Logs produced by pipeline runs inside the data directory.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.log


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Cloud-sync conflict copies. OneDrive, Dropbox and Box create these when the
# same file is edited in two places; they are duplicates, never real data.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*conflicted copy*
*Conflict*
